> @you06 @cfzjywxk What do you think? Do we need to fix it to be consistent with the behavior of MYSQL?

It's unexpected because the generated point get plan used index `u0`, 
```
+-------------------+---------+------+------------------------------+---------------+
| id                | estRows | task | access object                | operator info |
+-------------------+---------+------+------------------------------+---------------+
| Update_2          | N/A     | root |                              | N/A           |
| └─Point_Get_1     | 1.00    | root | table:t, index:u0(id, v, vv) | lock          |
+-------------------+---------+------+------------------------------+---------------+
```
Actually the primary key(which is handle key) could be used to access the row data directly, if it's used there will be a row returned instead of zero, and this statement will be blocked. Seems this is related to https://github.com/pingcap/tidb/blob/master/planner/core/point_get_plan.go#L784 this constraint generating the point get plan.

