Consider the following cases, if we relax the conditions by removing the `id = 1`, the update statement will not be blocked instead.

```sql
/* init */ drop table if exists t;
/* init */ create table t (id int primary key, v int, vv int, vvv int, unique key u0(v, vv));
/* init */ insert into t values(1, 1, 1, 1);

/* t1 */ begin;
/* t2 */ begin;
